@startuml
' NewEra POS - System sequence diagram of UC2 Handle Returns (main scenario and refund variants), W08
' Team D - editable source of assets/ssd_uc2.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng assets/ssd_uc2.puml
' Step numbers refer to UC2 in docs/requirements/SRS.md (W08 review changes, #28, #37, #50).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam ActorBorderColor #444444
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title NewEra POS - System sequence diagram: UC2 Handle Returns

actor ":Cashier" as Cashier
participant ":NewEra POS" as POS <<system>>

note over Cashier, POS
  Precondition: a cashier session is open (UC4) and the sale was made with UC1.
  The Customer takes part only through the Cashier.
end note

== Start the return (UC2 steps 2-3) ==
Cashier -> POS : makeNewReturn()
activate POS
POS --> Cashier : new return opened
deactivate POS

== Find the original sale (steps 4-5) ==
Cashier -> POS : findSale(receiptNumber)
activate POS
POS --> Cashier : sale line items with quantity bought\nand quantity already returned
deactivate POS
note right of POS
  Extensions: no sale with this receipt number (4a);
  no receipt, so no refund (4b);
  sale older than the refund period, return refused (5a).
end note

== Select the returned items (steps 6-7) ==
loop until all returned items are entered
  Cashier -> POS : enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, condition)
  activate POS
  POS --> Cashier : return line item, refund total (price paid + tax\nof the original sale), tender of the original sale
  deactivate POS
end
note right of POS
  The refund uses the price and the tax of the original sale:
  no call to the Tax Calculator. The condition is resellable
  or not resellable. Item not in the sale or quantity too large (6a)
  is rejected. Remove a line (6b) or cancel the return (8a)
  before confirming.
end note

== Confirm and refund (steps 8-11) ==
Cashier -> POS : confirmReturn()
activate POS
alt original sale paid in cash (9a)
  POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), return receipt
  deactivate POS
else original sale paid by credit card (9b)
  note right of POS
    The POS sends the refund request, with a transaction ID,
    to the Payment Service.
  end note
  alt refund approved
    POS --> Cashier : card refund done, return receipt
    deactivate POS
  else declined (9b2a)
    POS --> Cashier : reason; no cash is paid, a store manager must approve a cash refund
    deactivate POS
    Cashier -> POS : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason)
    activate POS
    POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), return receipt
    deactivate POS
  else no answer (9b2b)
    POS --> Cashier : no cash is paid; the POS asks for the refund status\n(confirmed, failed as 9b2a, or pending: confirmed later)
    deactivate POS
  end
else original sale paid by check (9c, Could)
  POS --> Cashier : a check cannot be refunded in cash without approval
  deactivate POS
  Cashier -> POS : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason)
  activate POS
  POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), return receipt
  deactivate POS
end

note over Cashier, POS
  After the refund the POS saves the return, increases the stock of the resellable items,
  queues the AccountingRecord and prints the return receipt (steps 10-11).
end note
@enduml
